  "description": "ICUROP crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P n n m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H128 Mn8 N28 O48 Y4,4(C5 H5 N1),2(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 10 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 10 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.802-3.825 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.36-128.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Y2Mn4(O2CCH3)(NO3)2(shi)4(O)(OH)](C5H5N)8(C3H7NO)3(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
